HBO might be best known for producing  hit series like The Sopranos Westworld  and Game of Thrones but the pay cable  network has consistently churned out  quality television series far beyond as  most popular programs some of its finest  works have been forgotten by time even  though many of them still hold up if  you're looking for another old show  stream to fill the void until all those  dragons and the theme park hosts are  back in action again here are some of  the hidden HBO gems you should take a  look at Angels in America when it  debuted back in 2003 Angels in America  was a unique television experience and  it still is the six-part miniseries was  adapted from the two-part play by Tony  Kushner and tells the story of the AIDS  crisis through a magical realist lens  the miniseries centers on a gay man  whose partner abandons him after he's  diagnosed with AIDS as if that weren't  enough of a burden  he's also visited by an angel who  declares him a prophet the series  features an all-star cast that includes  Justin Kirk Ben Shenkman mary-louise  Parker Emma Thompson Al Pacino Patrick  Wilson Jeffrey Wright and Meryl Streep  in multiple roles including a brief  stint as a mail rabbi bored to death  there's nothing else quite like bored to  death a comedy that began in 2009 and  ran for three seasons it stars Jason  Schwartzman as a writer who decides to  distract himself from the daunting  prospect of his next novel by becoming  an unlicensed private detective Zach  Galifianakis plays his best friend a  comic book artist and Ted Danson appears  as an older friend and mentor who edits  an acclaimed magazine where Jonathan  writes oh my god I have completely  failed at the most important thing in  life Jonathan doesn't take his detective  work all that seriously having learned  everything he knows from Raymond  Chandler novels but as the series goes  on he gets involved in some surprisingly  dire situations this show isn't for  everybody  but if you're a mystery fan or enjoy  comedies about overeducated stoners  failing at things it might be for you  carnival HBO is known for its ambitious  original programming and carnival is a  show that aims incredibly high but never  got fully off the ground however that  doesn't mean it's not an interesting  oddity worth of watch  especially for fans of dark fantasy set  in the Dust Bowl of the mid 1930s  carnival is about a traveling carnival  but it's also a supernatural battle  between destined avatars of good and  evil when the series started in 2003  creator Daniel Nava intended it to tell  one complex story over the course of six  seasons and fortunately HBO only ended  up giving it to so most of that story  remains untold but come back this Lisa  Kudrow comedy run for just two seasons  but spanned the nine years the former  friend star stars with a shallow and  self-centered 90s sitcom star trying to  make a return to the fame game with the  new sitcom and reality show unlike  Phoebe Buffay Kudrow's new character is  obsessed with her own image but  constantly fails to make a good  impression  despite her and likeability the series  also effectively satirizes a sexist and  ageist entertainment industry which has  little room and even less respect for a  middle-aged sitcom actress the comeback  was initially canceled after its first  season in 2005 but in the years to come  its reputation grow in 2014 the show was  unexpectedly revived for a second season  the comeback was an insightful and  biting satire from the start but the  long arc enabled by such an unusual  break between seasons makes it something  truly special we can only hope it  returns for a third season in 2023 five  days this 2007 co-production with the  BBC is a mystery series that also serves  as an effective emotional drama each of  the five episodes tells the story of one  day in the investigation of the  mysterious disappearance of a younger  mother and her two children spanning  from the very first day to the 79th day  of the search for truth this method not  only allows the audience to see how much  changes as the days weeks and months  roll on but it also introduces a  riveting performance by future Selma Sir  David Oh yellow Lowe who appears as a  father whose family vanishes parades end  Benedict Cumberbatch fans will  definitely want to check out parades end  which centers on three people whose  lives in Britain are upended by World  War one opposite Rebecca Hall and  Adelaide Clemens Cumberbatch plays a  rich conservative status dish  who is badly injured in the war the  entire five episode miniseries was  written by acclaimed playwright Tom  Stoppard and directed by Susannah white  and serves as a formidable British  period drama togetherness titans of  indie filmmaking brothers Mark and Jay  Duplass collaborated with Steve's assess  to create the plot for togetherness  which premiered in 2015 and run for two  seasons  mark Duplass plays Brett Pierson a Los  Angeles sound editor with a wife and two  kids melanie lynskey plays his wife  Michelle who's concerned about their  romantic life amanda peet is Tina Morris  Michelle's sister who unexpectedly moves  him with their family after splitting up  with her boyfriend in Houston zissis  appears as Alex Bret's best friend who  also moves in when his acting career  isn't going well  as anyone who's watched a television  show could guess an attraction develops  between Tina and Alex which gets  increasingly complicated as the show  goes on in other ways our starting with  the dialogue the show is quite unlike  the usual TV comedies and as two seasons  are well worth a look thanks for  watching click the loop icon to  subscribe to our YouTube channel plus  check out all this cool stuff we know  your love to  [Music]
 

